{
  "family": "window_lifecycle",
  "contract": "docs/parity/contracts/window_lifecycle.json",
  "canonical_commit": "e1825d40d52b4ae4f4bcb0b7e0dfc744dd20a452",
  "notes": [
    "Run with scripts/parity/capture_driver.py; REQUIRES --restart-cmd (persistence case).",
    "Window bookkeeping: session_setup creates windows A (fixture workspace host) and B; every case that creates a window closes it in its own state probe EXCEPT the two cli new-window cases, which cannot parse the created uuid from stdout and deliberately leak exactly 2 windows. The final case drains to the last window by session ids + window.list index placeholders (expects exactly 5 windows at its start: boot + A + B + 2 cli leaks) and pins canonical last-window close behavior under CMUX_UI_TEST_MODE, whatever it is (veto-with-ok or app termination); it is last so any termination cannot damage other cases.",
    "surface.resume set cases pass explicit cwd=/tmp/parity-cwd and source so binding payloads stay platform-neutral; resume_binding.updated_at is a wall-clock stamp (run-scoped timing nondeterminism, same class as the sanctioned events timing normalization) and is approved per case by JSON pointer.",
    "cli window displays stdout and display-not-found stderr embed physical display names (platform hardware) and are approved by pointer; exit codes stay strict.",
    "NOT ENCODED (with reason): surface.refresh dock branch (canonical fixture pins 'Dock placement is disabled' - no public op constructs a Dock); window.close notification-clear side effects (no public read exposes notification state); closed-window history recording/suppression (no public read); window geometry/cascade/styleMask defaults (not socket-observable); real key-window OS foregrounding and window.keyed/unkeyed on true key transfer (platform_equivalent per contract; captured only incidentally in events lanes); blocking resume-approval alert variants (canonical bypasses under test harnesses; only promptless paths encoded); remote-tmux window-close detach (no remote fixture); window.display happy move (needs a real display name; only error paths + listing encoded); snapshot-not-saved-during-termination adversarial (cannot deterministically order termination vs close; the persistence case forces a save via a scratch window close instead).",
    "INCIDENT (canonical run 29248166966): a surface.resume.set with source 'process-detected' (rewritten to 'manual') raised the BLOCKING resume-approval NSAlert on the canonical main actor (the XCTest bypass does not apply under CMUX_UI_TEST_MODE) and wedged every subsequent main-actor socket op (empty v2 replies, CLI timeouts) - the 13 PlaceholderErrors in that run were all downstream of this single wedge, not placeholder-shape bugs. REMOVED surface_resume.process_detected_rewritten_manual (the process-detected->manual rewrite quirk is not headlessly pinnable without the approval prompt) and surface_resume.auto_resume_agent_hook_honored (agent-hook + auto_resume:true is the auto-restore proposal path, the same blocking-prompt risk); the cli-source forced-false case remains (promptless CLI path). These join the approval-alert items in the not-encodable list."
  ],
